WEBVTT

00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:10.334
(Gasps, babbles) Oh!

00:00:14.959 --> 00:00:17.209
Good morning, Paddington.
Did you sleep well?

00:00:17.334 --> 00:00:19.875
I keep having the strangest dream.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Has anyone seen Mr Hunter?

00:00:22.125 --> 00:00:24.084
I'd like to know
if he's translated the bracelet.

00:00:24.209 --> 00:00:27.000
Or perhaps made us some breakfast.

00:00:27.125 --> 00:00:29.417
It's after ten, Mary!

00:00:29.542 --> 00:00:32.542
Hello?
Any chance of some coffee?

00:00:33.375 --> 00:00:37.417
It clearly states that breakfast
is served between 8:30 and 10:30.

00:00:38.417 --> 00:00:41.542
- Good morning, gentlemen... and madam.
- (Mr Brown keeps muttering)

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:43.917
Hello?

00:00:44.042 --> 00:00:45.750
Mr Hunter?

00:00:45.875 --> 00:00:47.334
Gina?

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:51.584
Is it me or is it getting a bit choppy?

00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:55.750
- (♪ Piano strikes up)
- Ooh!

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.167
(♪ Johann Strauss II's "Blue Danube Waltz"
playing on piano)

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:01.334
(Paddington grunting)

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:05.625
Marmalade!

00:01:11.417 --> 00:01:14.500
Shouldn't someone be driving?

00:01:15.625 --> 00:01:17.084
(Feedback on PA system)

00:01:17.209 --> 00:01:19.084
Gina? Mr Hunter?

00:01:20.459 --> 00:01:23.209
Ah! Better make an announcement!

00:01:25.167 --> 00:01:27.042
(Grunting)

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:29.667
There we... go! Oh! Ooh!

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:39.542
(Groaning)

00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:41.459
Oh!

00:01:41.584 --> 00:01:42.584
Huh!

00:01:43.584 --> 00:01:44.625
Oh, dear!

00:01:45.167 --> 00:01:49.959
Good morning. Please, could the Brown family
pop up to the front of the boat

00:01:50.084 --> 00:01:53.959
- for a slight, uh... emergency.
- Huh?

00:01:57.417 --> 00:02:00.000
- Left a bit...
- (Groaning)

00:02:00.125 --> 00:02:02.625
- Right a bit.
- Paddington!

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:05.042
(Paddington) Rather a lot of rocks!

00:02:05.167 --> 00:02:08.167
Paddington, what on earth
are you doing in there?

00:02:08.292 --> 00:02:11.042
I appear to be driving the boat,
Mrs Brown.

00:02:11.167 --> 00:02:13.417
- But where's Gina?
- She's not here!

00:02:13.542 --> 00:02:15.459
I don't think Mr Hunter's here either!

00:02:15.584 --> 00:02:18.334
Paddington, put it in reverse,
put the boat in reverse!

00:02:18.459 --> 00:02:19.917
Good idea!

00:02:20.042 --> 00:02:22.250
Reverse... That'll do it!

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:24.500
- (Engine speeding up)
- (Paddington) Oh!

00:02:24.625 --> 00:02:26.375
- (All groaning)
- That's faster!

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.542
Get the lifejackets!

00:02:34.709 --> 00:02:37.542
Where's Paddington?
Isn't he at the wheel?

00:02:37.667 --> 00:02:39.334
(Paddington) No! I appear to be...

00:02:40.375 --> 00:02:43.209
...on the wheel!
Clear the decks!

00:02:45.084 --> 00:02:49.292
Henry, the lifejackets!
Here! Emergency supplies!

00:02:50.042 --> 00:02:51.084
What?

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:56.834
- Hang on, Paddington.
- (Paddington groaning)

00:02:56.959 --> 00:02:58.584
Come back!

00:03:00.125 --> 00:03:01.667
Found the lifejackets!

00:03:01.792 --> 00:03:03.500
Abandon ship?

00:03:03.625 --> 00:03:05.750
Yes! Abandon ship!
Come on!

00:03:09.542 --> 00:03:12.375
Come on, everybody.
Three, two, one... jump!

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:14.334
Aunt Lucy's glasses!

00:03:16.917 --> 00:03:19.834
(Wailing)

00:03:23.334 --> 00:03:26.125
Grab hold of anything that floats!

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.375
Triple-laminated.

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:35.792
Wait... Paddington!

00:03:35.917 --> 00:03:37.167
- Paddington!
- Where is he?

00:03:37.292 --> 00:03:38.750
Where's Paddington?

00:03:38.875 --> 00:03:40.792
Paddington!

00:03:41.375 --> 00:03:43.125
(Gasping for air)

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:45.542
Found them! Good piano!

00:03:46.209 --> 00:03:48.625
Paddington!

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:50.292
Come on.

00:03:57.125 --> 00:03:59.584
(Judy) Day Three.
With the Browns lost in the jungle,

00:03:59.709 --> 00:04:02.125
everyone was thinking the same thing.

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:03.875
How long till we eat each other?

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:06.417
(Mr Brown) That's not helpful, Judy.

00:04:06.542 --> 00:04:09.125
Whoop! Mmm!

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:10.584
(Grunting)

00:04:10.709 --> 00:04:13.417
(Mrs Brown) Well, we wanted
a holiday to remember!

00:04:13.542 --> 00:04:15.584
At this rate, we may not be around
to remember it.

00:04:15.709 --> 00:04:20.000
Maybe we should just draw a big SOS
in the sand and chill here?

00:04:21.125 --> 00:04:22.542
"Chill here"?

00:04:22.667 --> 00:04:25.000
This is the Amazon,
not a shopping centre!

00:04:25.125 --> 00:04:27.375
All we need is a... plan!

00:04:30.792 --> 00:04:33.125
I have a plan, Mrs Brown.

00:04:33.959 --> 00:04:35.792
Mm-hmm?

00:04:35.917 --> 00:04:37.500
Um...

00:04:37.625 --> 00:04:40.625
We find Rumi Rock ourselves.

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:43.625
It can't be far, and whatever's happened
to Hunter and Gina,

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:46.167
they're bound to look for us there.

00:04:46.292 --> 00:04:48.584
Are you sure you can find the way?

00:04:48.709 --> 00:04:51.209
You have spent rather a long time
in London, Paddington.

00:04:51.334 --> 00:04:54.875
Mr Brown, you can take the bear
out of the jungle,

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.834
but you can't take the jungle
out of the bear.

00:04:57.959 --> 00:04:59.917
- (Animal growling)
- (Paddington gasps)

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:02.834
- Uh... anyway, follow me.
- Yes.

00:05:02.959 --> 00:05:05.292
Oh, and remember, whatever you do...

00:05:06.334 --> 00:05:08.209
...never touch this plant.

00:05:08.334 --> 00:05:11.292
- What's it called?
- The Spiky Red One.

00:05:12.459 --> 00:05:15.584
This'll be fun,
a short stroll in the jungle.

00:05:17.167 --> 00:05:19.792
(Mr Brown) And we're sure
this is a good idea, are we?

00:05:19.917 --> 00:05:22.917
(Mrs Brown) I don't think it's gonna be
that far to get to Rumi Rock. It can't be!

00:05:23.042 --> 00:05:25.625
People have gone there in the past.

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:31.459
(Phone ringing)

00:05:33.792 --> 00:05:37.125
(Scoffs) What is wrong with this thing?

00:05:42.792 --> 00:05:44.917
What have we here?

00:05:46.084 --> 00:05:48.792
Oh! Very strange!

00:05:48.917 --> 00:05:51.167
(Woman) It's Bingo time!

00:05:51.292 --> 00:05:55.209
- Oh, pardon.
- (Woman) Eyes down for a full house!

00:05:56.209 --> 00:05:59.792
- Noah's Ark, all the twos!
- Ooh!

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:03.459
- Days and nights, 40!
- Ooh, I got one!

00:06:05.625 --> 00:06:07.584
(Woman) All the horsemen...

00:06:07.709 --> 00:06:11.375
Horsemen of the Apocalypse,
number four.

00:06:13.292 --> 00:06:16.584
The Holy Trinity, number three.

